<misterromdescription>
  <name>Bubble Memories (bb3be, alt program)</name>
  <setname>bubblembe</setname>
  <year>1995</year>
  <manufacturer>Taito</manufacturer>
  <rbf>TaitoF3</rbf>
  <players>2</players>
  <joystick>8-way</joystick>
  <rotation>horizontal</rotation>
  <region>World</region>

  <!-- ============================================================
       UNTESTED. The ROM set has never been loaded by this core and
       none of the self-test expectations for it are measured, so the
       checksum rows report what they find rather than pass or fail.
       See PREP-BUBBLE.md for what must be measured first.

       Taito F3, the same board Ray Force runs on. Like Bubble Bobble
       II this set uses f3_224a - 224 lines from line 31, exactly Ray
       Force's crop - and extend 1, which the renderer is hardwired
       to. It is HORIZONTAL (MAME ROT0): set Rotate to None.
       MAME's sprite lag is 1, not Ray Force's 2.

       THE ONE STRUCTURAL DIFFERENCE FROM EVERY SET THE CORE HAS RUN:
       this game has NO sprites_hi ROM. MAME declares the region with
       EMPTY_SPRITE_HIDATA(0x200000), i.e. 2 MB of zeros, so its
       sprites are effectively 4bpp where every other set is 6bpp.
       That looked like the risk in this set and it is NOT: with that
       region all zeros, the reference model renders frames 900, 1200
       and 1800 of this game pixel-identical to MAME. The 4bpp path
       is correct. See PREP-BUBBLE.md for the gap that IS open (a
       sprite block/multi case, in the model, affecting both games).

       Sizes: this set FILLS maincpu (2 MB) and sprites (4 MB)
       exactly, where Ray Force pads both to half. Any future set
       larger than these needs the universal map extended.

       The universal F3 SDRAM map:

         0x0000000  maincpu    2 MB   4-way byte interleave (exact)
         0x0200000  audiocpu 512 KB   16-bit interleave (68000)
         0x0280000  sprites    4 MB   16-bit interleave (exact)
         0x0680000  sprites_hi 2 MB   ZEROS - no ROM in this set
         0x0880000  tilemap    4 MB   LOAD32_WORD pair (2 MB + pad)
         0x0C80000  tilemap_hi 2 MB   (1 MB + pad)
         0x0E80000  ensoniq    4 MB   2x 2 MB, plain
         0x1280000             = 18.5 MB total
       ============================================================ -->
    <!-- bubblembe: Bubble Memories with a DIFFERENT 68020 program. Every
       graphics and sound ROM matches the stock bubblem set byte for byte
       (CRCs verified against MAME 0.288 taito_f3.cpp), but all four maincpu
       ROMs are absent from MAME entirely, so this is an unofficial variant:
       a hack, patch or translation, not a documented clone.

       CONSEQUENCE FOR THE SELF-TEST PAGE: game id 3 carries measured
       expectations for STOCK bubblem, and a different program changes the
       assembled stream. ROM CHECKSUM, SDRAM BIST and WRITE HASH will read
       FAIL on this set and that is correct behaviour, not a fault. The
       measured values for THIS set are recorded below.
  -->
  <rom index="0" zip="bubblembe.zip" md5="None">

    <!-- maincpu: ROM_LOAD32_BYTE x4, 512 KB each - fills 2 MB -->
    <interleave output="32">
      <part name="e21-21.20" crc="c4a1e3c2" map="0001"/>
      <part name="e21-20.19" crc="bd9c3812" map="0010"/>
      <part name="e21-19.18" crc="c5a6ec87" map="0100"/>
      <part name="e21-18.17" crc="a15e492d" map="1000"/>
    </interleave>

    <!-- audiocpu 68000: ROM_LOAD16_BYTE pair -->
    <interleave output="16">
      <part name="e21-12.32" crc="34093de1" map="01"/>
      <part name="e21-13.33" crc="9e9ec437" map="10"/>
    </interleave>

    <!-- sprites: ROM_LOAD16_BYTE pair, 2 MB each - fills 4 MB -->
    <interleave output="16">
      <part name="e21-02.rom" crc="b7cb9232" map="01"/>
      <part name="e21-01.rom" crc="a11f2f99" map="10"/>
    </interleave>

    <!-- sprites_hi: THIS SET HAS NONE. MAME's EMPTY_SPRITE_HIDATA
         is an ERASE00 region, so the slot is 2 MB of zeros. -->
    <part repeat="2097152">00</part>

    <!-- tilemap: ROM_LOAD32_WORD pair -->
    <interleave output="32">
      <part name="e21-07.rom" crc="7789bf7c" map="0021"/>
      <part name="e21-06.rom" crc="997fc0d7" map="2100"/>
    </interleave>

    <!-- pad: tilemap 2 MB -> 4 MB -->
    <part repeat="2097152">00</part>

    <!-- tilemap_hi -->
    <part name="e21-05.rom" crc="07eab58f"/>

    <!-- pad: tilemap_hi 1 MB -> 2 MB -->
    <part repeat="1048576">00</part>

    <!-- ensoniq sample ROMs, plain (MAME 0x000000 and 0x400000;
         the lane spread is the core's job) -->
    <part name="e21-03.rom" crc="54c5f83d"/>
    <part name="e21-04.rom" crc="e5af2a2d"/>
  </rom>

  <!-- Game config (Rayforce.sv "GAME CONFIG"):
         bit [1:0] = 0  visarea f3_224a (224 lines from 31), as Ray Force
         bit [7:6] = 3  game id: expectations for this set are not
                        measured yet. NOTE that this is the LAST id the
                        field can hold - cfg_game is 2 bits, and
                        0/1/2/3 are Ray Force, Elevator Action Returns,
                        Bubble Bobble II and this. A fifth game needs
                        the field widened in Rayforce.sv.
         bits [2] and [4:3] (extend, sprite lag) are reserved and not
         read; left 0 as in the other MRAs. True values: extend 1,
         lag 1. -->
  <rom index="1">
    <part>60</part>
  </rom>

  <!-- Index 2 bits [2:0] = 4, with index 1 bits [7:6]=1 and [5]=1, encode
       game id 37: {idx2[2:0], idx1[5], idx1[7:6]} = {100,1,01}. Its own id,
       not stock bubblem's 3, so the self-test page judges this set's stream
       against its own measured checksum instead of reporting a false FAIL. -->
  <rom index="2">
    <part>04</part>
  </rom>


  <!-- the 93C46 settings EEPROM: 64 words, plus the 128-byte high
       score snapshot = 256. MAME ships a default EEPROM for this set
       (bubblem.nv, crc 9a59326e) which this MRA does NOT supply; the
       first boot writes its own defaults instead. -->
  <nvram index="254" size="256"/>

  <buttons names="Shot,Jump,-,-,-,-,Start,Coin,Service,Pause" default="A,B,R,L,Select,Start" count="2"/>
</misterromdescription>
